2026-08-03 - Offline AI journaling speech spike verified on Pixel 6a
- Decision/change: Added a Capacitor/Java/JNI voice-reflection bridge backed by official whisper.cpp v1.8.5 and the 59.7 MB English Base Q5_1 model. The Journal screen now records locally, transcribes after Stop, and places the raw transcript into an editable draft; no audio or text is uploaded.
- Device result: The official 11-second JFK sample transcribed accurately in 4.814 seconds on the connected Pixel 6a after enabling release optimisation and ARMv8.2 dot-product/FP16 instructions. The unoptimised debug baseline was 149.218 seconds. Measured proportional memory during the baseline was about 190 MB and phone temperature remained 31.2 C during two optimised runs. Android build and instrumentation test passed.
- Preserve/avoid: Keep record-then-transcribe for the first version rather than lag-prone live streaming. Keep the model outside Git/APK during the spike, verify its SHA-256 (`4BAF70DD0D7C4247BA2B81FAFD9C01005AC77C2F9EF064E00DCF195D0E2FDD2F`), compile only arm64-v8a, retain 16 KB ELF alignment, and do not add a paid cloud dependency.
- Model-formatting next step: Compare Qwen3 0.6B, Qwen3 1.7B, and Gemma 3 1B with the locked supplied 1,520-word transcript in a private Hugging Face ZeroGPU Space, then rerun finalists as the exact phone quantisations before integrating llama.cpp.
- Key files: android/app/src/main/cpp/, android/app/src/main/java/com/zenchad/minddojo/WhisperJournalPlugin.java, src/native.ts, src/screens/JournalScreen.tsx, experiments/journal-model-eval/.

